[Chapter "Slow Slav (4.e3)"]
[Line "Bd3 offers the trade"]
[Opening "Slav Defense: Quiet Variation, Schallopp Defense"]

{White offers to swap light-squared bishops. Black accepts and gets a very solid position.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 {Develop and guard d5 again.} 4. e3 Bf5 {Bishop out before ...e6.} 5. Bd3 {White offers to trade the bishops.} 5... Bxd3 {Take: trading off White's good bishop is welcome.} 6. Qxd3 e6 {A solid pawn chain, with the bad-bishop problem already solved.} 7. Nc3 Nbd7 {Develop and prepare a later ...c5 or ...e5.} 8. O-O Be7 {Develop and castle next: Black is very comfortable.} *
